            <ArticleTitle>An unusual case of groin discomfort.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>484-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Groin complications after cardiac catheterizations are common. With the increasing use of mechanical hemostatic devices, cardiologists must be alert to a wide array of potential problems. We report an unusual complication after the use of a closure device.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
